V-cycle over 4 exported levels, iterated 5 times. The learned smoother acts at level 3
only; coarser levels use damped Jacobi, because a fixed-length branch
cannot be applied at another DoF count or ordering.
A single V-cycle is one step of a stationary iteration; the loss
covers one smoothing pass plus one EXACT coarse solve, so the loss
being small does not by itself imply the recursive cycle contracts.
  learned@L3 + Jacobi below          first 0.1076 | after 5: 0.00897 | worst sample 0.0325
